  "rule1Title": "Have a complete trading plan before trading",
  "rule1Explanation": "A trading plan must include: market analysis, entry and exit points, risk management, and performance evaluation criteria. Without a plan, you are gambling, not trading.",
  "rule2Title": "Never risk more than 1-2% of capital on a single trade",
  "rule2Explanation": "This rule protects you from catastrophic losses. If you have $10,000, your maximum loss per trade should be $100-200. This allows you to survive a losing streak.",
  "rule3Title": "Follow the trading plan without exceptions",
  "rule3Explanation": "Emotions are the trader's worst enemy. Fear and greed will make you make irrational decisions. A well-designed plan eliminates emotion from the equation.",
  "rule4Title": "Wait for confirmation before entering",
  "rule4Explanation": "Don't anticipate the move. Wait for the price to confirm your analysis. Premature entry can result in an unnecessary stop loss.",
  "rule5Title": "Define stop loss and take profit BEFORE entering",
  "rule5Explanation": "Knowing exactly where to exit before entering allows you to calculate risk/reward and make objective decisions. Never move your stop loss down.",
  "rule6Title": "Don't trade when emotional",
  "rule6Explanation": "If you are frustrated by a loss, anxious, or euphoric from a win, your judgment is compromised. Take a break and come back when calm.",
  "rule7Title": "Always use stop loss",
  "rule7Explanation": "The market can move against you more than you imagine. A stop loss is your insurance against disaster. Without it, one trade can wipe out your account.",
  "rule8Title": "Analyze multiple timeframes",
  "rule8Explanation": "Before entering, check the trend on higher timeframes. A 15-minute entry should align with the 4-hour and daily trend.",
  "rule9Title": "Only trade with money you can afford to lose",
  "rule9Explanation": "Trading with rent money or emergency funds will put you under extreme emotional pressure. Trading requires risk capital, not essential funds.",
  "rule10Title": "Keep a trading journal",
  "rule10Explanation": "Record each trade: entry, exit, reason, emotion, result. Analyze patterns in your mistakes and successes. Improvement comes from analysis, not more trades.",
  "rule11Title": "The market is always right",
